%% Fixture for the opt-in recipes layer.
%%
%% Nothing here is a registered container word, which is exactly the point: the
%% engine renders every one of these as a generic div or span, and recipes.css
%% is the only thing that knows what they mean. Rendering them here ties the
%% class the engine EMITS to the class the CSS TARGETS, so a rename on either
%% side fails the gate instead of silently rendering unstyled.

# Recipes

{.lead}
An opening paragraph, set apart by an attribute line rather than by a construct
of its own.

## Tree

::: tree
- src/
  - parser/
    - blocks.crv
    - inline.crv
  - render/
    - html.crv
- tests/
:::

{data-guides="dotted"}
::: tree
- docs/
  - index.crv
:::

## Cards

::: cards
- *Parse* - source to AST.
- *Render* - AST to a target.
- *Format* - AST back to source.
:::

## Columns

{data-columns="3"}
::: columns
Three columns of running text, flowed rather than laid out.

The count comes from an attribute, so one class covers every arity.
:::

